{0 Expression to stack machine}

This library exposes the parts of the compiler from {e expression
language} to an instruction set for a {e stack machine}. The code
is organised into the following set of modules.


- {!Stackmachine.Ast}: The {e abstract syntax tree} for the expression
  language and relevant functions.

- {!Stackmachine.Machine}: The {e stack machine} instruction set
  together with facility to {e pretty print} using the
  {!Stackmachine.Machine.Pretty} module and a simulator given by
  {!Stackmachine.Machine.Simulator}

- {!Stackmachine.Translate}: This module contains the heart of the
  compiler which does the translation form expressions to instruction.


Besides there are parser ({!Stackmachine.Parser}) and lexer
{!Stackmachine.Lexer}) modules which are generated from the
corresponding menhir source file [parser.mly] and ocamllex source file
[lexer.mll] files.

The actual compiler executable uses this library and is essentially
just a driver program.
